ote":"Reconheça: I’ve → /aɪv/, she’s → /ʃiz/, wouldn’t’ve, whaddaya (what do you), gonna, wanna.","words":["I’ve been there.","She’s been studying.","What do you want?","I’d’ve gone."]}]}]},{"tag":"Fala","title":"Speaking","blocks":[{"type":"speak","title":"Speaking","prompts":[{"q":"Use success in a sentence.","pt":"Use.","model":"Hard work leads to success."},{"q":"Describe a successful person.","pt":"Descreva.","model":"She is a successful teacher."},{"q":"Use successfully.","pt":"Use.","model":"I successfully finished the course."}]}]},{"tag":"Escrita","title":"Writing","blocks":[{"type":"write","task":"Write 5 sentences with the succeed family.","model":"He succeeded in baking perfect bread. He was a successful baker. His success was in the bread. She successfully guessed the gift. Friendship needs sharing.","checklist":["Usei **succeed/success/successful/successfully**","Usei **succeed in + -ing**","5 frases"],"words":"5 frases"}]},{"tag":"Revisão e exame","title":"Review · Exam strategy · Teacher’s note","blocks":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Check yourself","items":[{"q":"What does “quiet neighbor” mean?","opts":["pão fresco","porta do vizinho","vizinho quieto"],"ans":2,"why":"**quiet neighbor** = vizinho quieto."},{"q":"What does “fresh loaf” mean?","opts":["pão fresco","pão da manhã","padeiro solitário"],"ans":0,"why":"**fresh loaf** = pão fresco."},{"q":"What does “morning bread” mean?","opts":["porta do vizinho","pão da manhã","padaria da esquina"],"ans":1,"why":"**morning bread** = pão da manhã."},{"q":"What does “neighbor’s door” mean?","opts":["padeiro solitário","forno de padaria","porta do vizinho"],"ans":2,"why":"**neighbor’s door** = porta do vizinho."}]},{"type":"box","kind":"exam","t":"Estratégia para as provas","body":["Treine esta habilidade com o formato de tarefas curtas das provas (TOEFL/IELTS).","Leia o enunciado primeiro e procure as palavras-chave."]},{"type":"box","kind":"teach","t":"Nota para o futuro professor","body":["Use exemplos reais d